            "review_text": "Tim G\nTay Ninh, Vietnam80 contributions\n0\nSurprised with the reviews\nOct 2019 • Couples\nI am a bit surprised with the reviews. My wife and I frequent the restaurant quite often, mainly due to the proximity to where we live and work, however I must admit we have limited ourselves to appetizers and cold Tiger beers. I would say the entree prices are a bit on the high side but the appetizers are average yet the quality and taste are very good. The draft Tiger beer has got to be the coldest in town served in frosty glass mugs! Anna, who I believe is a manager or supervisor speaks English very well and has always recommended food items that were “spot on”! I think it is a great place to stop and relax/recharge after visiting the War Remnants Museum if you are in the area.\nRead more\nWritten October 9, 2019",
